# PLATFORM-OWNED — written into the build context as `.dockerignore`.
#
# The context builder already excludes these when packing the tar, so this is the second
# belt: if a path ever slips into the archive, Docker still refuses to send it to the
# build. Cheap, and the failure it prevents (a snapshot's `.env` baked into an image
# layer, where it survives every later deletion) is not cheap.

.git
.gitignore
.bial-extract-ok

node_modules
.next
out
build

.env
.env.*

*.b64
app.bundle
npm-debug.log*
*.tsbuildinfo

# The platform supplies its own; an agent-authored one is never used.
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.*
.dockerignore
